Code-reading note (not a defect): the code comment claiming "renderChart mutates its argument
in place ... which would otherwise corrupt trendsChartRaw" is imprecise — charts.js:178-181
reassigns `data.data` to a new mapped array (spread-copied trace objects) rather than mutating
trace objects in place — but the underlying concern is real: if renderTrendsChart ever called
`renderChart('chart-trends', trendsChartRaw)` directly (bypassing filterTrendTraces's deep
copy), that reassignment would still corrupt trendsChartRaw.data by permanently swapping x/y.
The implementation correctly always routes through filterTrendTraces first, so this is a wording
nit, not a functional defect.

